From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add license-files glob to pick up licenses/ dir

pyproject.toml only sets the legacy `license = {text = "LGPLv3+"}` form
and never declares `license-files`, so setuptools' default
`LICEN[CS]E*`/`COPYING*`/`NOTICE*`/`AUTHORS*` root-glob never matches the
project's actual licence texts, which live under `licenses/*.txt`
(BSD_LICENSE.txt, LGPL_LICENSE.txt, MIT_LICENSE.txt) rather than at the
project root. Confirmed against the real published wheel
(sep_pjw-1.3.8-cp312-cp312-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux2014_x86_64.whl):
its dist-info carries no licenses/ directory at all, only AUTHORS.md.
Declaring `license-files = ["licenses/*.txt"]` makes setuptools carry
them into `dist-info/licenses/` with no other packaging change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against PJ-Watson/sep-pjw]
---
 pyproject.toml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@ classifiers=[
     "Intended Audience :: Science/Research",
 ]
 requires-python = ">=3.9"
+license-files = ["licenses/*.txt"]
 dependencies = [
     "numpy>=1.23.5",
     "sep>=1.4.0"
--
2.43.0
